%%begintext align
%% The 1. man cast off to his left-hand into the 2. wo. place, and the 2. wo cast up into the 2. man's place, then turn both
%% hands into their own places; then the 1. wo. cast off to her right-hand, into the 2. man's place, and the 2. man cast up into
%% the 1. wo. place, then take both hands and turn into their own places; then the two men lead through the two we. and
%% cross over into each other's places, and then hands round and come into each other's places again; then the we. go between
%% the men and cross over into each other's places and hands round.
%% [DMDfD]
%%endtext
%%sep 1 8 500
% Source: sources/jc/JohnWalsh/Britains.abc

